{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789820676,"nonce":"0HHcLzp6V4gSkPk4uWAA/cyzmyo=","title":"Warm-up thread compile races a first-call compile: Store finds no value in the map","message":"Running a Lua program through `zylua` (crates/zyntax_lua, branch worktree-lua-frontend) panics about one run in six with\n\n    thread 'zyntax-warm-up' panicked at crates/compiler/src/cranelift_backend.rs:\n    store in `zl_math_modf`: no value for its value HirId(49971)\n\nfollowed by `assertion failed: func_ctx.is_empty()` on the main thread, which was compiling a function of its own on first call at the same time. The function named varies between runs; it is always a library function the warm-up thread was compiling ahead of its first call.\n\nWith `ZYNTAX_DISABLE_WARM_UP=1` the same program is stable over dozens of runs, so the warm-up compile and the first-call compile interleave on backend state the value map is part of.\n\nReproducer: any Lua program touching `math` (the `zl_lib_math` table references every wrapper, so several dozen library functions become warm-up candidates), e.g.\n\n    local count = 0\n    for i = math.maxinteger - 2, math.maxinteger do count = count + 1 end\n    print(count)\n\nrun as `target/debug/zylua run t.lua` repeatedly.\n\nThe Lua conformance runner sets `ZYNTAX_DISABLE_WARM_UP=1` until this is fixed.","files":null}]}